# ----- Quick guide to install arch linux with a rice -----


# ----- Bigger Font

- setfont ter-132n

# ----- Check Wi-Fi Connection (SKIP IF ETHERNET)

My laptop has built-in wifi. I will use iwctl. Then it will penters us to the IWD terminal:

- iwctl

# ----- IWD Terminal

See list of networks:

- device list

# ----- WLAN0 Info -----

- device wlan0 show

# ----- See List Of Wi-Fi Networks

- station wlan0 get-networks

# ----- Connect To Wi-Fi

- station wlan0 connect <name of wifi> 
- password
-exit
- ping -c 4 google.com

# ----- Synchronize System Packages and Upgrade Them To Latest Version

- pacman -Sy

# ----- Format Disk & Prepare For Install

- lsbk:
  - View a list of connected drives
  - Confirm correct drive to use
  - Enter gdisk
    - gdisk /dev/<drive>
      - Enter x to enter expert mode
      - Enter z to erase the drive
      - Follow prompt, erase drive

# ----- Verify The Authenticity & Integrity Of Arch Linux Packages. Ensures They Come From Trusted Sources

- pacman -Sy archlinux-keyring

# ----- Set Up Arch Linux Install Script

- pacman -Sy archinstall

# ----- Launch Installer

- archinstall
  - Language
  - Disk Configuration
    - Partitioning
      - Best-effort
      - Select drive
        - Filesystem
          - btrfs
            - Compression
  - Encrypt if you want to
  - Bootloader
    - Grub
  - Hostname
  - Root Password
  - User Account
  - Profile
    - Type
      - Desktop
      - Hyprland
      - polkit
    - Graphics driver
      - Nvidia (proprietary)
  - Audio
    - pipewire
  - Network configuration
    - NetworkManager
  - Additional packages if you want to
  - Timezone
  - Install
      






